{title: A Time for Everything}
{subtitle: Ecclesiastes 3}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
For everything there is a sea[F/A]son
A time for [Gm7]every matter under heaven
A time to [Bb]be born, and a [F/A]time to die
A time to plant, [Gm7]and a time to uproot what was plant[Eb]ed
A time to [Cm7]tear down, and a [Fsus4]time to [F]build
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He has made ev[F]erything beautiful in its [Gm]time
E[Eb]ternity set [F]in our hearts
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [F] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A time [Bb]to weep, and a time to [F/A]laugh
A time to [Gm7]mourn, and a time to [Eb]dance
A time to em[Bb]brace, and a time [F/A]to let go
A time to keep [Gm7]silent, and a time to [Eb]speak
A time [Cm7]for war, and [F]a time for [Bb]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He has made ev[F]erything beautiful in its [Gm7]time
E[Eb]ternity set [F]in our hearts
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [F] | [Gm7] | [Eb] [F] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Everything beautiful [Gm]in [Eb]its [F]time
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [F] | [Gm] | [Eb] [F] | ×2
| [Bb] |
